      "id": 1,
      "text": "Downsville was founded in 1855 and platted in 1859, taking its name from Captain Downs.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        3,
        4
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downsville%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Downsville is tucked along the banks of the Red Cedar River, where the Red Cedar State Trail runs right into town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20,
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://discoverdownsvillewi.com/"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Captain Downs succeeded in building a dam in 1857 that powered a sawmill for the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Downsville%2C_Wisconsin"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Downsville and the Chippewa Valley were traditionally the home of the Santee Dakota and Ojibwe people.",
